<title>CHILE: Chile forex reserves end 1996 at $15.47 billion.</title>
<headline>Chile forex reserves end 1996 at $15.47 billion.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's foreign reserves rose $217 million in December to end the year at $15.47 billion, the Central Bank reported.</p>
<p>The gain was derived from a balance of payments surplus of $323 million, minus a $106 million reduction in the value of reserves due to currency exchange rate fluctuations, the bank said in its biweekly report.</p>
<p>-- Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211</p>
